      ],
      "name": "abdominal aorta",
      "entityType": "structure",
      "status": "canonical",
      "definition": "The abdominal aorta is the portion of the main artery situated below the diaphragm and above the common iliac arteries. It serves as the primary vessel distributing oxygenated blood to organs within the abdomen and pelvis.",
