      ],
      "name": "abdominopelvic cavity",
      "entityType": "structure",
      "status": "canonical",
      "definition": "The abdominopelvic cavity is a major division of the anterior body cavity housing abdominal and pelvic viscera. It encompasses both the abdomen proper and the pelvis, separated by an imaginary line between the hip bones.",
