      ],
      "name": "abducens nerve",
      "entityType": "structure",
      "status": "canonical",
      "definition": "The abducens nerve is the sixth cranial nerve responsible for controlling specific extraocular muscles. Its primary function involves contracting a muscle that moves the eye laterally away from its resting position.",
