        "skos:Concept",
        "stemma:Concept"
      ],
      "name": "abduction",
      "entityType": "process",
      "status": "canonical",
      "definition": "Abduction describes the movement of a bone away from the midline of the body. This action increases the angle between the limb and the central axis, occurring primarily at joints such as the shoulder or hip.",
