      ],
      "name": "abductor pollicis brevis",
      "entityType": "structure",
      "status": "canonical",
      "definition": "The abductor pollicis brevis is a superficial muscle in the thenar eminence that moves the thumb away from the palm. It originates on the scaphoid and trapezium bones to facilitate abduction of the first digit.",
