      ],
      "name": "translation",
      "entityType": "process",
      "status": "canonical",
      "definition": "Translation is the process through which RNA directs the formation of specific proteins within cellular machinery. During this stage, ribosomes read genetic codes to assemble amino acids into polypeptide chains that fold into functional structures.",
