      "name": "accuracy",
      "entityType": "concept",
      "status": "canonical",
      "definition": "Accuracy describes how closely a measured value aligns with the true or accepted correct standard. This property distinguishes precision from correctness, as high accuracy requires minimal systematic error in experimental results.",
