      ],
      "name": "acid ionization",
      "entityType": "process",
      "status": "canonical",
      "definition": "Acid ionization is the proton-transfer reaction in which an acid donates a hydrogen ion to water. The products are a hydronium cation and the acid's conjugate base, a shift that increases solution acidity.",
