      "name": "active electrode",
      "entityType": "structure",
      "status": "canonical",
      "definition": "An active electrode functions as a direct participant in the redox chemistry of an electrochemical cell, acting either as a reactant or product. Consequently, its physical mass diminishes or increases throughout the reaction process due to material consumption or deposition.",
