      "name": "Doppler effect",
      "entityType": "phenomenon",
      "status": "canonical",
      "definition": "The Doppler effect describes the shift in radiation frequency caused by relative motion between source and observer. When an object moves away, wavelengths stretch to redshift; approaching objects compress waves into blueshift, allowing astronomers to measure stellar velocities.",
      "provenance": {
        "aiDrafted": true,
