      "name": "exoplanet",
      "entityType": "concept",
      "status": "canonical",
      "definition": "An exoplanet is any planet that orbits a star other than the Sun. These celestial bodies exist in diverse systems across our galaxy, often detected through indirect methods like transit photometry or radial velocity measurements of their host stars.",
