      "name": "Kuiper belt",
      "entityType": "structure",
      "status": "canonical",
      "definition": "The Kuiper belt constitutes a region of space located beyond Neptune that maintains dynamic stability similar to the asteroid belt. It serves as the primary source region for most short-period comets found in our solar system.",
