      "name": "main sequence",
      "entityType": "concept",
      "status": "canonical",
      "definition": "The main sequence is a distinct band on the Hertzsprung–Russell diagram containing most known stars. It represents a stable phase where stars fuse hydrogen into helium in their cores, running diagonally from hot blue to cool red types.",
