      "name": "nebula",
      "entityType": "structure",
      "status": "canonical",
      "definition": "A nebula consists of a vast cloud composed primarily of interstellar gas or dust. These structures often glow visibly in infrared light, serving as stellar nurseries where new stars frequently form.",
