      "name": "normalization",
      "entityType": "process",
      "status": "canonical",
      "definition": "Normalization is a data preprocessing technique that scales numerical values into a consistent range, typically between zero and one. By eliminating scale differences across variables, this method facilitates accurate comparisons and improves the performance of machine learning algorithms.",
