      "entityType": "technique",
      "status": "canonical",
      "definition": "A development practice that exercises the smallest testable pieces of a program in isolation, usually individual functions or methods, against expected outcomes. Automated unit suites run quickly, localize defects, and support safe refactoring, though they do not replace integration or end-to-end tests.",
